{"name":"Gemini","hex":"#b4d6cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Gemini","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A constellation of the zodiac traditionally taken to represent the pair of twins Castor and Pollux in Greek mythology. It contains the stars Castor, Pollux, and Alhena.","The zodiac sign for the twins, ruled by Mercury and covering May 22 – June 21 (tropical astrology) or June 16 – July 15 (sidereal astrology)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who has the Gemini star sign.","A pair of something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gemini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gemini (constellation)","blocks":[{"text":"Gemini is one of the constellations of the zodiac and is located in the northern celestial hemisphere. It was one of the 48 constellations described by the 2nd century AD astronomer Ptolemy, and it remains one of the 88 modern constellations today. Its name is Latin for twins, and it is associated with the twins Castor and Pollux in Greek mythology. Its old astronomical symbol is  (♊︎)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Gemini_IAU.svg/330px-Gemini_IAU.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gemini_(constellation)","wikidata":"Q8923"},{"title":"Gemini (astrology)","blocks":[{"text":"Gemini is the third astrological sign in the zodiac. Under the tropical zodiac, the sun transits this zodiac sign between about May 22 to June 21. Gemini is represented by the twins, Castor and Pollux, known as the Dioscuri in Greek mythology. It is known as a positive, mutable sign. The opposite sign of Gemini is Sagittarius."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Gemini_symbol_%28bold%29.svg/330px-Gemini_symbol_%28bold%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gemini_(astrology)","wikidata":"Q129214"},{"title":"Gemini (language model)","blocks":[{"text":"Gemini is a family of multimodal large language models (LLMs) developed by Google DeepMind, and the successor to LaMDA and PaLM 2. Comprising Gemini Pro, Gemini Deep Think, Gemini Flash, and Gemini Flash Lite, it was announced on December 6, 2023. It powers the Gemini chatbot, and was named after the Latin word for \"twins\" and NASA's Project Gemini."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gemini_(language_model)","wikidata":"Q123688361"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/GeminiCC.jpg/500px-GeminiCC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/GeminiCC.jpg/500px-GeminiCC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The constellation Gemini as it can be seen with the unaided eye, with added connecting lines.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeminiCC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff/lossy-page1-1280px-Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Gemini_%28Annotated%29_%28gemini-ann%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The constellation Gemini showing the IAU boundaries, the constellation stick figure, and labels for its brightest stars. Astrophotograph by Eckhard Slawik, from NOIRLab's 88 Constellations project.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil